From: IntelXe (Claude Opus 5.5)
Subject: anv: video decode: DPB slot indices never corrupt the stack or stop the client

vkCmdDecodeVideoKHR's decode paths indexed arrays by slotIndex with only an assert: anv_h265_decode_video's
dpb_idx[16] (written for every reference slot, read through the RefPicSet* entries of StdVideoDecodeH265PictureInfo,
handed to the HuC S2L parameters) and anv_h264_decode_video's dpb_slots[17]; the AV1 path's prev_refs[9] is guarded.
By the reference number they index 16-entry arrays and the HuC S2L parameters' PicOrderCntValList[15] and
RefIdxMapping[15], and H.265 writes ReferencePictureAddress[hcp_ref_idx] with up to 16 active references into 8
entries. A slotIndex at or above the session's maxDpbSlots is invalid usage, but FFmpeg's H.264/H.265 Vulkan
hwaccels up to 9.0.2 number slots by their own DPB array index: 16 on the JCT-VC streams RPS_B_qualcomm_5,
RPS_C_ericsson_5, RPS_E_qualcomm_5 (a 16-picture DPB), 19 on the JVT streams HCBP2_HHI_A / HCMP1_HHI_A. On an Arc B580
the H.265 ones aborted the decoding process in __stack_chk_fail under anv_h265_decode_video <- gfx20_CmdDecodeVideoKHR.

Refusing such a decode is not an answer either: a first version of this patch left it unrecorded and set
VK_ERROR_INVALID_VIDEO_STD_PARAMETERS_KHR on the command buffer; FFmpeg 9.0.2 then never submitted, its execution's
fence stayed reset, and the decoder hung at the next use of that execution context (B580: all five streams).

For H.264 and H.265 the slot index is only a key (each reference is addressed through its picture resource; the
index ties pReferenceSlots to the RefPicSet* entries, and becomes H.264's 16-bit PictureID). dpb_idx and dpb_slots
are now tables of ANV_VIDEO_DECODE_SLOT_KEYS (256) entries: any uint8_t RefPicSet* entry is a valid read, any index
below 256 a valid write, and those streams decode as the client meant. CmdDecodeVideoKHR first makes a sanitized copy
of the decode info: a reference whose index is beyond the codec's table (256; AV1 9) or past the references the codec
path holds (H.264 16, H.265 15: the HuC parameters' size, which a 16-picture DPB never exceeds) is left out and decodes
as a missing reference; a VP9 inter frame whose reference names are not all in pReferenceSlots (anv_vp9_get_ref_idx
returned 0xff and the decode read pReferenceSlots[255]) is not recorded. H.265 keeps at most 8 active references.
Each case logs once (mesa_logw_once). No error is set: the command buffer ends with VK_SUCCESS, the submission
happens and signals the client's semaphores and fence. Negative indices are skipped as before. Encode is unchanged.

Platform independent. Applies on upstream f01e9b07a91 (with offsets) and on intelxe.diff (+ 0102-0105).

Generated-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/src/intel/vulkan/genX_cmd_video.c b/src/intel/vulkan/genX_cmd_video.c
index aa0f132..999474a 100644
--- a/src/intel/vulkan/genX_cmd_video.c
+++ b/src/intel/vulkan/genX_cmd_video.c
